Error: Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker: `.push()` changes `êntries`, which has read access only
  --> Tests/UI/dead_key_circumflex_parameter.jet:4:27
    |
  4 | add: fn(êntries: [Int]) { êntries.push(1) }
    |                           ^^^^^^^
 Why: On a keyboard layout where `^` is a dead key, `^` and the letter after it combine into one accented letter, so `^entries` was typed as `êntries`
 Fix: Write `entries: ^[Int]`; on a dead-key layout type `^` then a space, or switch to the layout's no-dead-keys variant
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker
